VERDICT: UNSUPPORTED -- this product does not implement Management Stacking.  The X960
TPS states it, and the DUT's own reads agree.  The product meets the same need with
Virtual Chassis Stacking (VCS) instead.
      the product statement ........... TPS row 236, Management Stacking = No
      the DUT agrees .................. one member, ID 1, Ready, Active Master, and
                                        `Operational Status: Stacking hardware disabled`
      what exists instead ............. a complete VCS configuration surface (STEP 2)
      device state changed ............ none.  Every command was a `show` or a `?` help
                                        probe, and no configuration command was sent

NEEDS:   To run this case as written, the product would have to offer Management
         Stacking: a way to manage several units as one management entity, separate from
         VCS.  It does not.
         To test the mechanism this product offers INSTEAD, a VCS test would need all of
         the following, and this bench can give none of it:
         1. A SECOND AT-x960-56YSQ, the same product as the DUT, on its own console and
            its own PDU outlet.  tb277 has no second unit of this product.
         2. BOTH units configured with `stack enable`, saved, and then RELOADED.  The DUT
            says so itself: `% Stacking is currently disabled, please save the config and
            reboot after enabling stacking`.
         3. A stacking link between the two units.
         The other two units on this bench cannot stand in.  swi_b is an AT-x960-28YSQ, a
         different model that does not share a switching core with the DUT.  swi_a is an
         AT-x950 GEN2-52XSTQm, a different product again.
         No bench change is requested, because no bench change could turn this verdict
         into a PASS.  The feature under test is one the product states it does not
         implement.  A second AT-x960-56YSQ would allow a VCS case to be written, and
         that would be a different case from this one.

