STEP 2 -- what the platform offers instead: the VCS configuration surface        done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: the TPS gives a reason for row 236 being No: "these units support VCS".  This
  step checks whether that reason is true on this DUT.  Configuration mode, `?` probes
  only.  Nothing was executed and nothing was created.

awplus(config)#stack ?
  <1-8>                       A specific stack member ID
  all                         all stack member configuration
  disabled-master-monitoring  Enables the resiliency-link monitoring when the
                              device is a Disabled-Master.
  enable                      Enable VCS hardware
  management                  VCS management VLAN configuration
  mixed-mode                  Set this stack member to be compatible with
                              other products
  resiliencylink              Resiliency link configuration for the stack
  virtual-chassis-id          VCS virtual chassis id
  virtual-mac                 Enable the virtual MAC address feature
awplus(config)#stack 1 ?
  priority                   Change the specified stack member priority value
  renumber                   Change the existing stack member ID
  software-auto-synchronize  stack member software version auto
                             synchronization
awplus(config)#stack management ?
  subnet  Subnet address of the VCS management VLAN
  vlan    VCS management VLAN
awplus(config)#stack enable ?
  <cr>
awplus#show stack ?
  detail          Detailed information display
  full-debug      Complete detailed debug information
  resiliencylink  Stack resiliency link information

  => STEP 2 done: the platform offers a complete VCS surface.  It can enable the stacking
     hardware, set a management VLAN and subnet, set a virtual chassis id, enable a
     virtual MAC, configure a resiliency link, set a member priority, renumber a member,
     synchronise software between members and run in mixed mode.  This is the mechanism
     the product provides in place of Management Stacking, exactly as TPS row 236 says.

STEP 3 -- a real VCS test, and why this bench cannot run one                   NOT RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The DUT states the condition itself:

awplus#show stack resiliencylink
  % Stacking is currently disabled, please save the config and reboot after enabling stacking.

  So a VCS test needs two units of the same product, both with `stack enable` saved, both
  reloaded, and a stacking link between them.  tb277 has one AT-x960-56YSQ.  swi_b is an
  AT-x960-28YSQ, a different model, and it does not share a switching core with the DUT.
  swi_a is an AT-x950 GEN2-52XSTQm, a different product again.  Enabling VCS on the DUT
  alone would need a save and a reload, and would produce a one-member stack, which is
  what the DUT already reports.
  => STEP 3 NOT RUN: there is no second unit of this product on this bench, so no VCS
     test could be run.  This does not affect the verdict.  The case asks about
     Management Stacking, which this product states it does not implement, and no bench
     change could alter that.
